{{!
    @template local_moodesk/ticket_detail_thread

    Ticket detail — the conversation. Rendered inside .mhd-detail__main by
    ticket_detail.mustache.

    Every entry keeps its own identity in the markup: an internal note, a system
    event, a reply reached across a merge link and the viewer's own messages all
    read differently, because an agent scanning the thread has to be able to tell
    at a glance whose message this is and who can see it.

    Context variables:
      * thread[]    - Array of thread entries. Each entry has: authorname, isnote, isown,
                      issystem, timecreated, message, hasattachments, and attachments[] where
                      each attachment exposes url, filename, and size. Entries that came from a
                      ticket merged into this one also carry islinked, linkedfrom (source ticket
                      id) and linkedurl.
      * isterminal  - True when the ticket is in a terminal state (renders end-of-conversation notice)

    Example context (json):
    {
      "isterminal": false,
      "thread": [
        {
          "authorname": "Jane Doe",
          "isnote": false,
          "isown": true,
          "issystem": false,
          "islinked": false,
          "timecreated": "8 May 2026, 10:30",
          "message": "<p>Looking into this now.</p>",
          "hasattachments": false
        }
      ]
    }
}}

{{! role="log", not on the scrollport around it: that one also holds the custom
    fields and the merged source fields, and turning those into a live region
    would have a screen reader announce administrative data as conversation.
    aria-relevant is narrowed to additions — an entry appearing is news, an edit
    inside one already read is not. The region's name comes from the scrollport,
    so this element is deliberately unnamed rather than named twice. }}
<div class="mhd-thread" role="log" aria-relevant="additions">
  {{#thread}}
  <article class="mhd-thread-entry{{#isnote}} mhd-thread-note{{/isnote}}{{#isown}} mhd-thread-own{{/isown}}{{#issystem}} mhd-thread-system{{/issystem}}{{#islinked}} mhd-thread-linked{{/islinked}}">
    <div class="mhd-thread-entry__head">
      <span class="mhd-thread-entry__author">
        <strong>{{authorname}}</strong>
        {{#isnote}}
        <span class="mhd-pill mhd-pill--warning">
          {{#str}} reply_internal_note_label, local_moodesk {{/str}}
        </span>
        {{/isnote}}
        {{#issystem}}
        <span class="mhd-pill mhd-pill--neutral">
          {{#str}} reply_system_event_label, local_moodesk {{/str}}
        </span>
        {{/issystem}}
        {{#islinked}}
        <a href="{{linkedurl}}" class="mhd-pill mhd-pill--link">
          {{#str}} merge_linked_reply_label, local_moodesk, {{linkedfrom}} {{/str}}
        </a>
        {{/islinked}}
      </span>
      <small class="mhd-thread-entry__time">{{timecreated}}</small>
    </div>
    <div class="mhd-thread-entry__body">
      {{{message}}}
      {{#hasattachments}}
      <ul class="mhd-attachment-list">
        {{#attachments}}
        <li>
          <a href="{{url}}" class="mhd-attachment-item" download>
            <span class="mhd-attachment-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="mhd-attachment-name">{{filename}}</span>
            <span class="mhd-attachment-size">{{size}}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        {{/attachments}}
      </ul>
      {{/hasattachments}}
    </div>
  </article>
  {{/thread}}

  {{#isterminal}}
  <p class="mhd-thread-terminal" role="note">
    {{#str}} ticket_terminal_notice, local_moodesk {{/str}}
  </p>
  {{/isterminal}}
</div>
